/* book: lead: An LTI system can be described by how it treats each frequency. If x(t) has Fourier transform X(ω), the output has Y(ω)=H(ω)X(ω). The complex number H(ω) is the frequency response. It scales amplitude by |H(ω)| and shifts phase by ∠H(ω). This turns time-domain convolution into multiplication in frequency. Engineers use it to read RC filters, audio tone controls, communication channels and control  */
